# Build-context excludes for `Dockerfile.test` ONLY.
#
# BuildKit uses `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` when it exists and that file
# REPLACES the root `.dockerignore` outright — the two are never merged.
#
# THAT LOOKUP IS BUILDKIT-ONLY. Podman and Buildah do not implement it: they
# read the root `.dockerignore` and this file is never consulted, so every
# test is stripped and the image builds green with nothing to run. Pass
# `--ignorefile Dockerfile.test.dockerignore` on those engines. A guard in
# Dockerfile.test fails the build when the test sources are missing, so this
# cannot pass silently again.
# So every exclude the root file needs, this file needs too, minus the
# ones the test image genuinely depends on.
#
# What this file deliberately does NOT exclude (and why it can't just be
# deleted in favour of the root file): `web/e2e`, `**/*.test.ts`,
# `**/*.spec.ts`, `**/__tests__`. The root `.dockerignore` drops all four
# because the prod runtime image must not ship tests; the test image is
# built to RUN them.

node_modules
web/node_modules
web/.svelte-kit
.git
.planning
agent/sessions
.playwright-mcp
TESTENV/
test-results/

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The root `.dockerignore` excludes these; because that file is REPLACED
# rather than merged (see header), omitting them here meant a host
# .env.prod / .pi-secret / agent auth token landed in this build's
# context. None are build inputs — the test image gets its config from
# docker-compose.test.yml `environment:`.
.env
.env.*
**/.pi-secret
**/.pi-salt
agent

# ── Local-only trees, never build inputs ───────────────────────────────
# The expensive omission. `worktrees` is path-exact, so both spellings
# are needed to also catch `.claude/worktrees/` — where the Agent tool's
# `isolation: "worktree"` writes. Measured together: 51 GB across ~10.9M
# files, none of it a build input. See the long note in `.dockerignore`.
worktrees
**/worktrees
**/node_modules
.claude
.cache
coverage
coverage-shard
.merge-snapshot
.wrangler
tasks
projects

# Runtime data, not a build input (DB dirs, extension state, snapshots).
**/.ezcorp
/data/
/web/data/
*.db
ez-corp-db
